<h1>The Collaborative Advocate Foundation</h1>
<p class="header-info">501(c)(3) Nonprofit Organization | EIN: 41-3618503</p>
<p class="header-info">17912 Stefano Drive, Pflugerville, TX 78660</p>
<p class="header-info" style="margin-bottom: 16pt;"><b>Additional Financial Context</b></p>

<p>The Collaborative Advocate Foundation (TCAF) is a newly formed 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization. FY2025-2026 represents our first fiscal year of operations. As such, we do not yet have two completed fiscal years of financial statements, nor has an IRS Form 990 been filed, as the organization has not completed its first full fiscal year.</p>

<p>TCAF's total operating budget for FY2025-2026 is $12,000, funded entirely through personal investment by the founder. No salaries have been drawn during this startup phase. The organization is fully volunteer-led.</p>

<p>Despite our early-stage financial position, TCAF has built substantial organizational assets during this period:</p>

<p><b>Technology Infrastructure:</b> A 24-platform digital ecosystem is live and operational, serving Central Texas communities across health equity, workforce development, education, veteran services, benefits navigation, and community data intelligence. Platforms include HerHealth Network (70+ women's health conditions with validated clinical screenings), Whole-Person Health (six clinical instruments including PHQ-9, GAD-7, C-SSRS), RPLICE (SDOH data integration by ZIP code), MentorConnect, Mission Transition, ThriveUp Academy, and 18 additional specialized platforms.</p>

<p><b>Implementation Science:</b> TCAF has developed a proprietary RPLICE implementation science engine operationalizing CFIR 2.0, RE-AIM, EPIS, and other evidence-based frameworks for program fidelity monitoring and continuous improvement.</p>

<p><b>Community Relationships:</b> TCAF's founder serves on the Pflugerville ISD School Health Advisory Council (SHAC) and maintains coalition partnerships across Central Texas.</p>

<p><b>Clinical Tools:</b> Six validated screening instruments and three platform-developed assessments are deployed across the ecosystem, with auto-escalation protocols for crisis intervention (988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline, Reach a Vet).</p>

<p>TCAF is actively pursuing grant funding to transition from founder-funded operations to sustainable programmatic delivery. The attached operating budget reflects our current financial position with full transparency. We believe our technology assets, community infrastructure, and operational readiness position TCAF to execute the proposed Sankofa Knowledge Systems project effectively with RWJF support.</p>

<p style="margin-top: 24pt;"><b>Prepared by:</b><br>
Dr. Terry Flood, DHA<br>
President<br>
The Collaborative Advocate Foundation</p>

